#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:5
msgid "構造最適化"
msgstr "Geometry Optimization"

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:7
msgid ""
"正方晶 BaTiO₃ の格子を固定し、原子座標を緩和すると、Ti と O の相対変位はどう変わるでしょうか。\\ OpenMX "
"を使った密度汎関数理論（DFT）の計算では、Ti の中心からのずれが残り、主に O 原子が動きました。\\ "
"機械学習原子間ポテンシャル（MLIP）でも極性変位が残りましたが、c 軸に沿う 2 本の Ti–O 結合の長さの差は、いずれも OpenMX "
"より大きくなりました。"
msgstr ""
"How do the relative displacements of Ti and O change when we relax the "
"atomic coordinates of tetragonal BaTiO₃ at a fixed lattice? \\  In "
"density functional theory (DFT) calculations with OpenMX, Ti remained "
"off-center and the O atoms accounted for most of the motion. \\  The "
"machine-learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs) also retained the polar "
"displacements, but all gave a larger difference between the lengths of "
"the 2 Ti–O bonds along the c axis than OpenMX did."

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:12
msgid "目的と背景"
msgstr "Objectives and Background"

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:14
msgid ""
"正方晶の BaTiO₃ では、理想立方晶からのわずかな格子ひずみと、Ti・O の相対変位が強誘電性に関わります。\\ BaTiO₃ "
"が正方晶構造をとることは、Megaw の実験で報告されました :sup:`[1]`。\\ 中性子散乱実験では相転移と\\ `ソフトモード "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/soft_mode.html>`__\\ "
"の関係が示されています :sup:`[2]`。\\ 第一原理計算では、Ti 3d 軌道と O 2p 軌道の混成が強誘電構造の安定化に重要とされます"
" :sup:`[3]`\\ （技術ノートの\\ `Ti 3d–O 2pの混成の役割 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectric_origin.html#fo-hybridization>`__）。"
msgstr ""
"In tetragonal BaTiO₃, ferroelectricity involves both a slight lattice "
"strain relative to the ideal cubic phase and relative displacements of Ti"
" and O. \\  Megaw reported the tetragonal crystal structure of BaTiO₃ "
"experimentally :sup:`[1]`. \\  The link between the phase transition and "
"\\  `soft modes <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/soft_mode.html>`__ \\  has been demonstrated by "
"neutron scattering experiments :sup:`[2]`. \\  First-principles "
"calculations indicate that hybridization between Ti 3d and O 2p orbitals "
"is important in stabilizing the ferroelectric structure :sup:`[3]` \\  "
"(see the Technical Notes on the \\  `role of Ti 3d–O 2p hybridization "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectric_origin.html#fo-"
"hybridization>`__)."

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:19
msgid ""
"この例では格子定数と格子角を固定し、OpenMX、CHGNet、SevenNet（モデル ``7net-mf-"
"ompa``）、FairChem（モデル ``uma-s-1p1``）で原子座標を緩和します（`固定セル緩和 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html"
"#structure-optimization>`__）。\\ どの原子がどれだけ動いたかは、各原子の初期座標を基準に調べます。\\ "
"緩和後の極性変位を手法間で比べるときは、Ba を基準にした Ti・O の変位と、酸素八面体の Ti–O 結合距離を見ます。"
msgstr ""
"In this example, we fix the lattice constants and angles and relax the "
"atomic coordinates with OpenMX, CHGNet, SevenNet (model ``7net-mf-"
"ompa``), and FairChem (model ``uma-s-1p1``) (see `fixed-cell relaxation "
"<https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html#structure-"
"optimization>`__). \\  We use each atom's initial coordinates as the "
"reference to determine which atoms move and by how much. \\  To compare "
"the relaxed polar displacements across methods, we examine the "
"displacements of Ti and O relative to Ba and the Ti–O bond lengths in the"
" oxygen octahedron."

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:26
msgid "入力ファイル例"
msgstr "Example Input Files"

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:28
msgid ""
"対象の手法のブロックを開き、入力ファイルをコピーします。\\ QE の入力例は :doc:`安定基底状態 <stability>` "
"で使った正方晶の設定です。\\ この記事に掲載する計算結果は、OpenMX、CHGNet、SevenNet、FairChem の 4 手法です。"
msgstr ""
"Open the block for the method you want and copy the input file. \\  The "
"QE example uses the tetragonal settings from :doc:`Stable Ground State "
"<stability>`. \\  The results in this article are for 4 methods: OpenMX, "
"CHGNet, SevenNet, and FairChem."

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:61
msgid "QE：固定格子・原子座標緩和"
msgstr "QE: Fixed-Lattice Relaxation of Atomic Coordinates"

#: ../../BaTiO3/geometry-optimization.rst:63
msgid ""
"以下は、:doc:`stability` で用いた正方晶相の QE 入力例を、この記事でもそのまま利用する場合の設定です。\\ Quloud "
"Job では、各ジョブに含まれる ``QuloudJob.scf.in`` を以下の例で置き換え、\\ ``calculation = "
"'relax'`` によって格子を固定したまま原子位置のみを最適化します。"
